Native ASCII geometry fixture
-----------------------------
designer-ascii-geometry.txt contains eight filtered records from Altium
Designer's ASCII save of the upstream PiDP11IOExpander.PcbDoc identified above.
The selected fields retain their original spellings, values, IDs and order.
Line endings have been normalized. The complete native ASCII save had SHA-256
f1cae67437698f5a0812729ef9bc1892266bd644ded128e599863b5acdb51b00.
The board outline and the three overlay arc centers were also measured through
the native PCB editor. This derived fixture is covered by the same BSD-2-Clause
license.

Altium report readings (altium-reports-reva.json)
-------------------------------------------------
Readings of three further files from the same RevA release zip (sha256 87c4064f...), made by
tests/support/altium-reports.cjs: the rule rows, counts and listed violations of
"Fabrication/Design Rules Check.html" (sha256 6ca049d16095ebba1bfc7c1f4748dd3b12ac85537157799dd30b39b177056f6c),
the messages of "Fabrication/Electrical Rules Check.html" (sha256 8d819428ca29a83efdd261cb7c0d3642e493db4916c84f2f95d1e3a3eac34004)
and the cells of "Assembly/Bill of Materials.xlsx" (sha256 77eb7feb32be2a72135146b353c85dd9354c3fb94f55b2d9f7b71253011d7c13).
The reports name a path on the author's machine, so only the readings are kept. With the full-tier
cache (tests/altium-fidelity/fetch.py) the suites read the originals again and require the same
readings. Used by tests/checks/drc-altium-report.cjs and tests/formats/bom-altium-report.cjs.
Same BSD-2-Clause terms as the release.
